{
    "background_story": "Mckenna was a dedicated social worker who had spent her entire career advocating for the underprivileged. Growing up in a low-income household, she had firsthand experience with the struggles of accessing quality healthcare. After witnessing her own family's difficulties, Mckenna became determined to make a difference. She spent years working with local non-profits, helping to enroll eligible individuals in Medicaid and connecting them with vital medical services. Her tireless efforts led to the creation of a community clinic, providing free healthcare to hundreds of families in need. Mckenna's selflessness and commitment to improving the lives of others earned her recognition as a leading voice in healthcare advocacy. Her work continued to inspire others to join the fight for equal access to medical care, leaving a lasting impact on her community.",
